§ `Planning Act 1998 -- enforcement and appeals`

§§ `21, 22 -- appeals and finality`

-- s 22(1): an applicant may appeal to the Minister against a refusal, a grant subject to conditions, or a conditional
-- provisional permission; (2) any person aggrieved by a cancellation. (3): "within 60 days of the date of the
-- notification of the decision". (4): an appeal does not suspend conditions or enforcement unless the Minister directs.
-- (7), (8): after the Minister decides, the competent authority may add conditions "not ... inconsistent with the
-- decision", and those may be appealed in turn. (9): "The decision of the Minister is final and is not to be challenged
-- or questioned in any court."
-- s 21(1), (4): the Minister may call in applications; a called-in decision "is final, and is not subject to appeal
-- under section 22 or to be challenged or questioned in any court".
DECLARE PlanningDecision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal`
    `a grant with conditions`
    `a conditional provisional permission`
    `a cancellation`
    `a called-in decision of the Minister`
    `a grant without conditions`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A PlanningDecision, `days since notification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister lies` IF
        `days since notification` AT MOST 60
    AND CONSIDER `the decision`
        WHEN `a called-in decision of the Minister` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a grant without conditions` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A PlanningDecision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may question the Minister's decision` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal against a refusal or conditions suspends enforcement` IF
    `the Minister directed otherwise`

§§ `28, 29, 30 -- enforcement notices`

-- s 28(5)(a): an enforcement notice must take effect not less than 14 DAYS after service. (6): it may be served on the
-- owner, the occupier, or anyone who appears responsible.
-- s 29(1): appeal to the Minister "at any time BEFORE the notice takes effect". (5): an appeal SUSPENDS the notice
-- unless the Minister directs otherwise. (4): the Minister's decision is final.
-- s 28(9): "Except by way of an appeal to the Minister under section 29, the validity of an enforcement notice is not to
-- be questioned in any court or proceedings whatsoever."
-- s 28(8): "Compliance with the requirements of an enforcement notice ... does not discharge the notice."
-- s 30(1): failing to comply -- the person served is guilty. (2): resuming the use, or reinstating demolished works,
-- after compliance is an offence "despite the earlier compliance". (3): $200,000 or 12 months, and $10,000 a day.
--
-- An enforcement-notice appeal suspends the notice (s 29(5)); a planning appeal does not suspend enforcement (s 22(4)).
-- And because compliance does not discharge the notice, it binds the land's use indefinitely, until superseded by a
-- permission or withdrawn (s 28(7)).
DECLARE NoticeAppeal HAS
    `days since service` IS A NUMBER
    `days until the notice takes effect` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the appeal` IS A NoticeAppeal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enforcement notice appeal is in time` IF
    `the appeal`'s `days since service` LESS THAN `the appeal`'s `days until the notice takes effect`

GIVEN `days from service to effect` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice gives the minimum period` IF
    `days from service to effect` AT LEAST 14

DECLARE NoticeStatus HAS
    `was served the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `complied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `later resumed the prohibited use or reinstated the works` IS A BOOLEAN
    `superseded by a permission or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the status` IS A NoticeStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits an enforcement notice offence` IF
        NOT `the status`'s `superseded by a permission or withdrawn`
    AND (    (`the status`'s `was served the notice` AND NOT `the status`'s `complied`)
         OR  `the status`'s `later resumed the prohibited use or reinstated the works`)

GIVEN `the status` IS A NoticeStatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compliance has discharged the notice` IF
    FALSE

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `an appeal to the Minister under section 29`
    `judicial review`
    `a defence in the prosecution`

GIVEN `the forum` IS A Forum
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice's validity may be questioned in the forum` IF
    CONSIDER `the forum`
    WHEN `an appeal to the Minister under section 29` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `34 -- paying a civil penalty instead of being prosecuted`

-- s 34(1): for granting a written permission in respect of development, works or subdivision for which an offence
-- appears to have been committed, the competent authority may require a penalty, "whether or not proceedings have been
-- instituted". (2): the penalty "must not exceed the lower of ... (a) 50 times the fee prescribed for an application ...;
-- (b) $150,000." (3): the authority's certificate of the amount is "conclusive". (4): once paid, "No further proceedings
-- are to be instituted or taken against any person for an offence under section 12".
--
-- The criminal maximum under s 12(4) is $200,000. The civil penalty to regularise is capped at $150,000, and paying it
-- stops the prosecution of anyone -- the text says "any person", not only the payer.
GIVEN `the application fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `the application fee` TIMES 50 LESS THAN 150000 THEN `the application fee` TIMES 50 ELSE 150000

GIVEN `the penalty has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person prosecuted is the payer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 12 prosecution may still proceed` IF
    NOT `the penalty has been paid`

§§ `42(3) -- a tenant who pays the owner's debt`

-- s 42(3): a tenant, subtenant or occupier who pays a sum due from the owner to avoid seizure or sale of the land may,
-- "in the absence of any written agreement to the contrary, deduct the amount so paid ... from the rent ... and may
-- retain possession thereof until that amount has been fully reimbursed".
GIVEN `paid the owner's debt to avoid sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `a written agreement says otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant may deduct it from rent and keep possession` IF
    `paid the owner's debt to avoid sale` AND NOT `a written agreement says otherwise`
